    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d980">

                <pb facs="1475" n="1461" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 LCC/16: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-15T16:00:00+01:00">February 15,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1264. Sir Orme Sargent states that instructions along the lines of paragraph 7 of
                    his letter of February 11 are being sent to the British Ambassador, Moscow. He
                    assumed that the American Ambassador will receive similar instructions from the
                        Department<anchor n="13" xml:id="d980-f1"/> (this refers to the Department’s
                    1120, February 14, 2 p.m.).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d980-f1" n="13" xml:id="d980-f1-content">
                <p>On February 16, 1944, the Department notified Ambassador Winant in telegram 1176,
                    8 p.m., as follows: “Harriman instructed.” (740.0011 LCC/16) Ambassador
                    Harriman’s instructions were sent in telegram 312, February 16, to Moscow
                    (740.0011 LCC/16a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
